  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uzbekistan Education for Excellence Program (under DOAG)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uzbekistan):  .The activity will support the Development Objective Grant Agreement between USAID and the Uzbekistan Ministry of Public Education (MPE) for Improved Education Outcomes.  The primary goal of the activity is to develop, test, implement, and evaluate effective and scalable education reforms that reach Uzbekistani pupils in public schools throughout the country.  To achieve this, the activity works in close coordination with MPE to develop high quality teaching and learning materials for Uzbek language arts, mathematics, ICT, and English as a foreign language (EFL), and transforms the way teachers are trained and instruction is delivered.  The activity will also develop methods and strategies to increase transparency and accountability in schools and improve school management and service delivery.  The activity will result in improved pupil learning.  FY 2021 funding will support the procurement, customization and printing of ICT and EFL student textbooks and teacher guides from international publishing companies.  This activity supports ICS Objective 4.2: Uzbekistan&apos;s educational institutions move into greater alignment with international norms in order to facilitate increased academic cooperation and exchange with U.S. institutions... .</narrative>
  </description>
